# Do not touch live application state

Never apply migrations, restart the server, or otherwise change the running
app or its live database and media.

```bash
# ❌ BAD
python manage.py migrate
python manage.py runserver

# ✅ GOOD
python manage.py makemigrations --dry-run --check
pytest tests/
```

Writing a migration file is fine. Applying it with `migrate` is not. Pytest
may use its own isolated test database; do not migrate, write, or delete
`db.sqlite3`, `ENTRY_FOLDER`, or anything the running server is using.
Leave live state for the user.
